BUNDLED IN THIS REPOSITORY

  lwext4            GPL-2         github.com/gkostka/lwext4
                    reads and writes ext4 without a kernel. Compiled into fwz, with one
                    local fix in tools/fwz/patches/
  miniz             MIT           github.com/richgel999/miniz
                    deflate, inflate and crc32. Compiled into fwz
  speex 1.2.1       BSD-3-Clause  xiph.org
                    the codec the intercom's telephony speaks. Sources vendored at
                    tools/ffmpeg-speex/vendor/speex with their COPYING, compiled into
                    ffmpeg-speex
  c300x-controller  Apache-2.0    github.com/slyoldfox/c300x-controller
                    the program that runs on the intercom. Shipped already built at
                    device/controller/bundle.js, from tag v2024.9.1 with the patches in
                    device/patches/


REDISTRIBUTED IN THIS PROJECT'S RELEASES

Copies of upstream files, byte for byte, because they go inside the firmware this project
builds. Each is verified against a pinned sha256 before use.

  node 17.9.1       MIT           nodejs.org
  go2rtc 1.9.14     MIT           github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc
  libatomic         GPL-3 + runtime exception, from the c300x-controller repository


DOWNLOADED WHEN BUILDING FROM SOURCE

Fetched against a pinned sha256, and needed only to build ffmpeg-speex.

  zig 0.16.0        MIT           ziglang.org
  ffmpeg 7.0.2      LGPL-2.1+     github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg at tag n7.0.2, unmodified


THE ffmpeg-speex BINARY THIS PROJECT PUBLISHES

Built from the ffmpeg 7.0.2 sources above and the vendored speex, with neither
--enable-gpl nor --enable-version3, so it is LGPL-2.1-or-later. tools/ffmpeg-speex/build.sh
is the exact recipe, and both sources are the ones named above.


